  "conclusion": "Only the factory post-enter?post-GetCurrentThreadId pair changes: native critical-section LockCount DWORD+4 is -2?-6, corresponding to0?1 waiting thread under the documented modern Windows bitfield. Native owner/recursion and game-owned wrapper bytes remain unchanged. This is consistent with contention by the observed background mixer thread, not evidence that GetCurrentThreadId writes the lock.",
  "limits": [
    "The native EnterCriticalSection entry/waiter increment is not instrumented: the exact writer/timing of that LockCount change is not independently isolated. It is recorded as a concurrent/unattributed transition.",
    "Mixer/factory post-Leave snapshots already show native/game-wrapper ownership by background TID20500; post-call state is not necessarily an unlocked main-thread-owned snapshot. Those bytes must not be assigned to a pure main-thread GetCurrentThreadId or LeaveCriticalSection implementation.",
    "The raw trace proves background mixer execution, actual GetCurrentThreadId target/return and observed main-thread service ordering. It does not establish whole-game thread scheduling or complete source factory/service replay.",
    "No installed file, native capture or earlier failed-inspection report was changed. No game or input/device probe was launched by this audit."
  ],
